.TH SJB 1 "2026-10-02" "sjb" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sjb \- terminal music player with streaming and offline libraries
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sjb
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B sjb \-\-offline
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B sjb \-\-path
.I directory
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B sjb \-\-import\-lrc
.I song_id file
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sjb
plays music from a SQLite catalog or a directory of local MP3 files.
It provides a terminal interface with genre browsing, search, a playback
queue, shuffle, playlists, lyrics, album artwork, and an audio visualizer.
Audio is decoded with FFmpeg and played through SDL.
.PP
Run without arguments to open the catalog.
A build installed with
.B "./build.sh \-\-system"
uses the catalog and configuration under
.IR ~/.sjb .
A development build uses paths relative to the current working directory.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-db " file"
Use the specified catalog instead of the default database.
Cannot be combined with
.B \-\-offline
or
.BR \-\-path .
.TP
.BI \-\-config " file"
Read the color theme from the specified Lua file.
A missing default theme is allowed; an explicitly selected theme must be readable.
.TP
.B \-\-offline
Scan and play downloaded MP3 files in
.IR ~/.sjb/songs .
The directory must already exist.
.TP
.BI \-\-path " directory"
Scan and play a local MP3 library rooted at
.IR directory .
This option selects offline mode.
See
.BR "LOCAL LIBRARIES" .
.TP
.BI \-\-cover " file"
Override the album artwork used during playback.
With
.BR \-\-preview ,
load a local PNG for the preview screen.
.TP
.B \-\-preview
Open the player layout with sample display data.
.TP
.BI \-\-import\-lrc " song_id file"
Import UTF-8 LRC lyrics into the selected library, replacing the song's
existing lyrics, then exit without opening the interactive player.
.I song_id
must be a positive database ID.
May be combined with
.B \-\-db
for a catalog, or with
.B \-\-offline
or
.B \-\-path
for a local library.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print usage information and exit.
.SH KEY BINDINGS
Keys are case-sensitive.
Available actions depend on the current screen; the footer shows controls
for that screen.
Printable keys enter text while editing a search, playlist name, or cover path.
.SS Navigation
.TP
.B "Arrow keys, h j k l"
Move through menus or adjust the selected control.
.TP
.B "Enter, Space"
Activate the selected item or control.
On the player screen, select the play/pause control to toggle playback.
.TP
.B "g, G"
Move to the first or last item.
.TP
.B "Esc, Backspace"
Close the current panel or return to the previous screen.
Backspace deletes text when editing.
.TP
.B "q, Ctrl-D"
Open the quit confirmation screen.
Cancel is selected by default.
Select Quit and press Enter or Space to exit; press Esc or q to cancel.
The home menu's Quit item and MPRIS quit requests use the same confirmation.
Playback continues while confirmation is open.
Signals such as Ctrl-C and a closed terminal still terminate immediately.
.TP
.B "1, 2, 3"
Show the player, lyrics, or visualizer.
.TP
.B Tab
Cycle through player, lyrics, and visualizer views.
.TP
.B s
Open search from the player, or edit search in the song list.
On the home, genres, and settings screens, switch between settings and genres.
.TP
.B Ctrl-U
Clear the text being edited.
.TP
.B t
Open or close the typewriter style panel, except in the visualizer.
.SS Playback and queue
.TP
.B "Up, Down"
Raise or lower volume in the player and visualizer when no panel is open.
In other contexts, move through the menu or lyrics.
.TP
.B Q
Open or close the queue.
Press Enter on a queue entry to play it.
.TP
.B n
Insert the highlighted song immediately after the current song.
Available in the song list and queue.
.TP
.B d
Download the highlighted catalog song in the song list, queue, or playlist,
or the current song from the player.
.TP
.B D
Download all songs in the catalog.
.SS Playlists
.TP
.B p
Open or close the playlists panel.
.TP
.B a
Choose a playlist to receive the selected song.
.TP
.B "c, r"
Create a playlist or rename the selected playlist in the playlist list.
.TP
.B x
Delete the selected playlist, or remove the selected song from an open playlist.
.TP
.B "K, J"
Move the selected playlist song up or down.
.TP
.B C
Edit the open playlist's cover path or URL.
.TP
.B "S, R"
Toggle shuffle or track repeat while browsing an open playlist.
.TP
.B "[, ]"
Play the previous or next track while browsing an open playlist.
.SH DOWNLOADS
Downloads are started with
.B d
or
.B D
inside the normal player; there is no download command-line option.
Only one download job runs at a time.
Playback and navigation remain available while it runs.
Completion and failure messages appear in the interface.
Quitting cancels the active download.
.PP
Songs are saved under
.IR ~/.sjb/songs ,
inside a subdirectory named for the first catalog genre, if one exists.
Songs without a genre are saved directly in the root.
Only validated MP3 responses are accepted.
Incomplete transfers are not added as playable songs.
.PP
Filenames use the database title followed by
.BR .mp3 ,
not a filename supplied by the server.
Path separators and control characters are replaced, and long components
are shortened to fit the filename scheme.
When a name is already occupied by another file, a song-ID suffix is used
to distinguish the download without overwriting it.
An existing valid download from the same source is reused.
.PP
A companion
.B .mp3.sjb
file records the catalog title, artist, album, and source URI.
Keep this file beside the MP3 to preserve catalog names in offline mode
even when the embedded tags differ.
.SH LOCAL LIBRARIES
The directory passed to
.B \-\-path
is the library root.
Each immediate subdirectory defines a genre using its directory name.
Tracks in deeper directories remain in the genre of that top-level directory.
MP3 files directly in the root have no genre and appear in
.BR All .
All also includes every track found in genre directories.
.PP
Files with a case-insensitive
.B .mp3
extension are inspected for MP3 audio.
Invalid files, hidden entries, and symbolic links are skipped.
Embedded title, artist, album, and cover data are used where available;
the filename supplies a title when no title tag is present.
Downloaded tracks use their companion catalog metadata in preference to tags.
.PP
The library is rescanned at startup.
Tracks that remain at the same path retain their IDs; missing tracks are
removed from the index.
Each library root has its own database and playlists under
.IR ~/.sjb/libraries .
Scanning a local directory does not modify the online catalog.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.sjb/jukebox.db
Default catalog for a system-installed build.
.TP
.I ~/.sjb/playlists.db
Saved playlists for the default installed catalog.
For a custom catalog, the playlist database is placed beside that catalog.
.TP
.I ~/.sjb/config/theme.lua
Default theme for a system-installed build.
Returns a Lua table containing a
.B colors
table with
.BR purple ,
.BR green ,
and
.B blue
values in
.B #RRGGBB
notation.
.TP
.IR jukebox.db ", " config/theme.lua
Default catalog and theme paths for a development build, relative to the
current working directory.
.TP
.I ~/.sjb/songs/
Downloaded MP3 files and companion metadata.
.TP
.I ~/.sjb/libraries/<root-hash>/jukebox.db
Index for the canonical path of a local library root.
.TP
.I ~/.sjb/libraries/<root-hash>/playlists.db
Playlists belonging to that local library.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOME
Home directory used for user data and installed defaults.
.TP
.B TERM
Terminal type.
Album artwork display requires
.BR xterm-kitty .
.TP
.B "TMUX, STY"
If either variable is set, terminal artwork display is disabled.
.SH EXAMPLES
Open the installed catalog:
.PP
.nf
.RS
sjb
.RE
.fi
.PP
Play downloaded songs:
.PP
.nf
.RS
sjb \-\-offline
.RE
.fi
.PP
Use a local music directory:
.PP
.nf
.RS
sjb \-\-path "$HOME/Music"
.RE
.fi
.PP
For this directory layout,
.B Loose Track
appears only in All;
.B Album Track
appears in both Rock and All:
.PP
.nf
.RS
Music/
    Loose Track.mp3
    Rock/
        Album Track.mp3
.RE
.fi
.PP
Import timed lyrics into a catalog:
.PP
.nf
.RS
sjb \-\-db ./jukebox.db \-\-import\-lrc 2 ./song.lrc
.RE
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal termination, successful lyrics import, or help output.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid arguments or an initialization, import, or terminal-input error.
.TP
.B 128 + signal number
Termination after a handled signal.
.SH NOTES
An interactive terminal is required for the player interface.
Artwork is optional; playback does not require a graphics-capable terminal.
MPRIS controls are exposed on the session D-Bus when available,
allowing compatible clients such as
.B playerctl
to control playback.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR playerctl (1),
.BR sqlite3 (1)
